# The quotas: all off, then Kiro's alone (kiro-cli chat --no-interactive /usage, which is
# fake-agent here: run with -Env FAKEACP_USAGE_MS=3000 for a read that takes a while as the
# real one does), then Codex's (no ~/.codex sessions in a fresh profile: a readable failure),
# then all four. Claude's and Cursor's read the network and the user's sign-ins: on a
# machine without them they fail readably too. Each read's child shows in samples.csv.
launch
expect "bench visible" 30 as startup
mark quotas-off
sleep 15

send quota kiro on
expect "bench ok" 5
mark quota-kiro-read
send until-quota kiro 40
expect "bench quota kiro" 45
mark quota-kiro-on
sleep 15

send quota kiro off
expect "bench ok" 5
send quota codex on
expect "bench ok" 5
send until-quota codex 20
expect "bench quota codex" 25
mark quota-codex-on
sleep 10

send quota kiro on
expect "bench ok" 5
send quota claude on
expect "bench ok" 5
send quota cursor on
expect "bench ok" 5
mark quota-all-read
send until-quota cursor 40
expect "bench quota" 45
send until-quota claude 40
expect "bench quota" 45
send until-quota kiro 40
expect "bench quota" 45
mark quota-all-on
sleep 15

send quota kiro off
expect "bench ok" 5
send quota codex off
expect "bench ok" 5
send quota claude off
expect "bench ok" 5
send quota cursor off
expect "bench ok" 5
mark quotas-off-again
sleep 15
mark -
quit 30
